# Emergent Haunting: Bot1 casts it on turn one (a spell cast from their hand, so no trigger at that end step: it stays an
# enchantment). On turn three Bot1 casts nothing, so at their end step the trigger goes on the stack and, resolving, makes it a
# 3/3 Spirit creature with flying in addition to being an enchantment, with no duration. On turn five it attacks: a Memnite
# cannot block it (flying) and it deals 3. At that end step it is already a creature, so the trigger does not go on the stack.

[Bot1 Deck]
Emergent Haunting
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x19

